cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HD-SMS: Hierarchical Delta Sparse Merkle Structuring — Executable Prototype"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the manuscript and this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahid
    given-names: Muhammad
repository-code: "https://github.com/blockchain2030/Hierarchical-Delta-Sparse-Merkle-Structuring-HD-SMS-"
abstract: >
  Reference Python implementation of Hierarchical Delta Sparse Merkle
  Structuring (HD-SMS), with a Sparse Merkle Tree baseline and a
  reproducible benchmark harness for micro-fraction token transfer
  workloads. All commitments use SHA-256 with domain separation; no
  experimental values are hardcoded in the source.
keywords:
  - blockchain
  - sparse merkle tree
  - authenticated data structures
  - delta encoding
  - micro-fraction transfers
  - layer-2 rollups
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-06-29
